  "body": "## Objective\n\nAdvance issue #16 from fixture-only registration checks to actual native OS lifecycle evidence in disposable GitHub-hosted environments. No service is installed on the creator's PC and no real organism SELF is changed.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- Add separate read-only-permission Windows/Linux Python 3.12 workflow with a ten-minute job bound and no provider secrets.\n- Opt-in test refuses normal local/self-hosted execution and keeps generated NESTs under RUNNER_TEMP.\n- Use production registration/removal, real local organ runtime and newly born disposable encrypted Body; require startup, communication, restart, already-stopped removal, preserved Primer/native bytes and VCW validity.\n- Linux tests automatic systemd on-failure restart following SIGKILL and zero-status cooperative stop. Windows tests explicit Task Scheduler forced stop/start, not graceful stop or automatic recovery.\n- Retain JUnit results only; preserve ownership checks during cleanup. Disposable hosted machines are discarded on failure.\n- Update PLAN.md, lifecycle evidence and changelog without changing production-completion claims.\n- Real Windows testing exposed omitted default RunLevel XML; accept absence but reject explicit elevated, empty or unknown values. Keep owner/action checks intact and mirror the correction into the Hermes seed.\n- Windows installation now immediately starts the verified task, matching Linux. The native test no longer supplies an initial task start. Verification/start failure retains pending intent and refuses unsafe execution or rollback.\n\n## Verification scope\n\nLocal code-quality and process regression checks run with native registration deliberately skipped. The new native workflow and existing full Windows/Linux matrix, security and pinned-Hermes gates must pass before merge. This PR does not close issue #16: login/reboot certification, Windows automatic restart, partial-removal recovery, storage fencing and crash-atomic admission remain open.\n\nLocal final regression: 194 passed, 3 platform/opt-in skips; Ruff, public audit and seed checksums passed. Both native jobs passed at commit 30647be; final head tightens immediate-start verification and must pass again. Both native checks have been added to protected-main requirements without removing any existing checks or app bindings.\n",
